{"name":"Bonfire","hex":"#f78058","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bonfire","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, controlled outdoor fire lit to celebrate something or as a signal.","A fire lit outdoors to burn unwanted items; originally , heretics or other offenders, or banned books; now, generally agricultural or garden waste, or rubbish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To destroy (something) by, or as if by, burning on a bonfire;  to burn or set alight.\n\n To fire (pottery) using a bonfire.\n\n To start a bonfire in (a place); to light up (a place) with a bonfire.","To destroy (something) by, or as if by, burning on a bonfire;  to burn or set alight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bonfire"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bonfire","blocks":[{"text":"A bonfire is a large and controlled outdoor fire, used for waste disposal or as part of a religious feast, such as Saint John's Eve."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Seurasaari-2005-johannus2.jpg/330px-Seurasaari-2005-johannus2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonfire","wikidata":"Q9505308"},{"title":"Bonfire (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Bonfire is a German hard rock/heavy metal band, founded by Hans Ziller in Ingolstadt, Upper Bavaria in 1972. In 1986, the band changed its name to Bonfire. Ziller remains a member and owns the rights of the name \"Bonfire\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Bonfire_Metal_Frenzy_2019_35.jpg/330px-Bonfire_Metal_Frenzy_2019_35.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonfire_(band)","wikidata":"Q682299"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Bonfire_2018%2C_The_Hague%2C_preparations_on_31_December_2017.jpg/500px-Bonfire_2018%2C_The_Hague%2C_preparations_on_31_December_2017.jpg?utm_so